From: op15-gki-kernel maintainers
Subject: [PATCH] sched: keep sched_schedstats off after init atrace.rc write

Android's /system/etc/init/atrace.rc writes 1 to
/proc/sys/kernel/sched_schedstats during late-init, enabling
sched_info accounting across all CPUs for the entire boot. Keep the
sched_schedstats static key disabled when PID 1 init performs that
boot-time write while leaving explicit non-init writes working and
CONFIG_SCHEDSTATS enabled for GKI KMI parity.
---
diff --git a/kernel/sched/core.c b/kernel/sched/core.c
--- a/kernel/sched/core.c	2026-11-23 00:13:34
+++ b/kernel/sched/core.c	2026-11-23 00:13:34
@@ -5237,8 +5237,12 @@
 	err = proc_dointvec_minmax(&t, write, buffer, lenp, ppos);
 	if (err < 0)
 		return err;
-	if (write)
+	if (write) {
+		/* Ignore PID 1 init's boot-time atrace.rc write; keep static key off unless enabled later. */
+		if (state && task_pid_nr(current) == 1)
+			return err;
 		set_schedstats(state);
+	}
 	return err;
 }
 #endif /* CONFIG_PROC_SYSCTL */
